{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/confluentinc/cp-schema-registry","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:05:23.844Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/confluentinc/cp-schema-registry/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/confluentinc/cp-schema-registry"},"readme":"# Confluent Docker Image for Schema Registry\n\nDocker image for deploying and running the Schema Registry. The source code is currently available on [Github](https://github.com/confluentinc/schema-registry-images/). \n\nPlease see the [Confluent Platform documentation](https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/installation/docker/installation.html) for documentation on these images - including quickstart guides, Docker Compose configs, reference documentation and advanced tutorials.\n\n# Resources\n\n[Schema Registry documentation](https://docs.confluent.io/current/schema-registry/index.html): installation and configuration, tutorial, and schema evolution and compatibility checking, and security.\n\n[Confluent Platform documentation](http://docs.confluent.io/current/cp-docker-images/docs/intro.html) on these images: quickstart guides, Docker Compose configs, reference documentation and advanced tutorials.\n\n[confluentinc/cp-demo](https://github.com/confluentinc/cp-demo): GitHub demo that you can run locally.  The demo uses this Docker image to showcase Confluent Schema Registry in a secured, end-to-end event streaming platform. It has an accompanying playbook that shows users how to use Confluent Control Center to manage and monitor Kafka connect, Schema Registry, REST Proxy, KSQL, and Kafka Streams.\n\n[confluentinc/examples](https://github.com/confluentinc/examples): additional curated examples in GitHub that you can run locally.\n\n# Contribute\n\nStart by reading our guidelines on contributing to this project found here.\n- Source Code: https://github.com/confluentinc/schema-registry-images\n- Issue Tracker: https://github.com/confluentinc/schema-registry-images/issues\n\n# License\n\nUsage of this image is subject to the license terms of the software contained within. Please refer to Confluent's Docker images documentation [reference](https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/installation/docker/image-reference.html) for further information. The software to extend and build the custom Docker images is available under the Apache 2.0 License. \n\n## Disclaimer\ns390x images are provided for IBM LinuxONE customers under IBM terms only. They are not covered under standard Confluent support.","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"confluentinc","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/confluentinc","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2016-07-22T01:01:31.750955Z","updated":"2026-09-16T15:07:20.345007Z","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":163582901,"stars":98},"mediaTypes":["application/octet-stream","application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json"],"contentTypes":["unrecognized","image"],"storage":714184347885,"tags":[{"name":"7.9.10","digest":"sha256:ae63c314e3f78f78d5bdce8c64c0f98ea1dc4d358ef52de2fdae56cda7e82ec0","pushed":"2026-09-16T15:07:19.896464Z","size":2188206170,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"7.9.10-1-ubi8","digest":"sha256:ae63c314e3f78f78d5bdce8c64c0f98ea1dc4d358ef52de2fdae56cda7e82ec0","pushed":"2026-09-16T15:07:15.524069Z","size":2188206170,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"7.8.11","digest":"sha256:5f43ed943b533c895a43b1a680fdae58fa0d15baba4a91606745ea9d83ad15ed","pushed":"2026-09-16T15:06:32.335339Z","size":2128829335,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"7.7